          %h3#duskins_monadicity_theorem Duskin’s monadicity theorem
          %p
            Duskin’s monadicity theorem gives a different sufficient condition, which is necessary under light conditions on the categories involved and which refers only to quotients of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
          %p
          #DuskinMonadicityTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Duskin monadicity theorem)
              %br/
              A functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon D \to C
              between finitely complete categories is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  has a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} creates
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                  whose
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/images"} images
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  have
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+coequalizers"} split coequalizers
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              admits all coequalizers of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+pairs"} contractible pairs
              then these conditions are also necessary.
          %p We can weaken the hypothesis a bit further to obtain the theorem:
          %ul
            %li
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              between finitely complete categories is monadic if it creates
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotients"} quotients
              for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruences"} congruences
          %p As usual, we can also modify it by replacing reflection of limits by reflection of isomorphisms.
          %ul
            %li
              A conservative right adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon D \to C
              between finitely complete categories is monadic if any congruence in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              which has a quotient in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              already has a quotient in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            If we view the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as underlying
            = succeed "-objects" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            induces a
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Duskin actually gave a slightly more precise version only assuming the categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            to have particular finite limits, rather than all of them.
          %h3#monadicity_over_set Monadicity over Set
          %p
            In the case when the base category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon D\to Set
            is monadic if and only if:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                has a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                admits
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel+pairs"} kernel pairs
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+pair"} parallel pair
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo ⇉
                      %mi S
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \rightrightarrows S
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is a kernel pair if and only if its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
                under
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is so,
            %li
              %p
                A morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to B
                in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
                if and only if its image under
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is so.
          %h3#strict_monadicity Strict monadicity
          %p
            The version of the monadicity theorem given in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} MacLane 1971
            uses a notion of “creation of limits” which fails to observe the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            %em isomorphism
            of categories, rather than merely an equivalence. But the versions mentioned above can be found in the exercises.
          %p
            Note however that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U: D \to C
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amnestic+functor"} amnestic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibration"} isofibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is monadic iff it is strictly monadic. For an application of this observation, see for example the discussion of algebraically free monads at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+monad"} free monad
          %h2#examples_and_applications Examples and Applications
          %h3#actions_over_sets Actions over sets
          %p
          #BaseChangeOfPresheavesAlongFullyFaithfulFunctor.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
                along
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective functor
              %br/
              Let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mphantom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo −
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\mathcal{S}
                    \\overset{\phantom{---}}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\mathcal{S}'
            %p
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
              which is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective"} essentially surjective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplete+category"} bicomplete category
              (e.g.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/precomposition"} precomposition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} categories of
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            #eq:BaseChangeOfPresheavesAsMonadicFunctor.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ;
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    PSh
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{S}
                    ;\,
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\big)
                    \\overset{\;\; F^\ast \;\;}{\longleftarrow}
                    PSh
                    \\big(
                    \\mathcal{S}'
                    ;\,
                    \\mathcal{C}
                    \\big)
            %p
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BeckMonadicityTheoremAlternative"}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  By the assumption that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicomplete+category"} bicomplete
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+extensions"} Kan extensions
                  of presheaves along
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  exist and exhibit
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\ast
                  as the middle part of a (“
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"}> base change
                  ”)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
                  \:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo !
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊣
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mo ;
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo ↔
                          %mphantom
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo −
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mo −
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mi 𝒮
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ;
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        F_! \,\dashv\, F^\ast \,\dashv\, F_\ast
                        \\;\;
                        \\colon
                        \\;\;
                        PSh
                        \\big(
                        \\mathcal{S}
                        ;\,
                        \\mathcal{C}
                        \\big)
                        \\overset{\phantom{----}}{\leftrightarrow}
                        PSh
                        \\big(
                        \\mathcal{S}'
                        ;\,
                        \\mathcal{C}
                        \\big)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This shows that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\ast
                  has a left adjoint. In addition, it
                  %em is
                  a left adjoint and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoints+preserve+colimits"} as such preserves all colimits
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coequalizers"} coequalizers
              %li
                %p
                  The assumption that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
                  implies that
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi F
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\ast
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
                  (because
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
                  of presheaves are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
                  of the underlying functors which are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  is an isomorphism.)
            %p
          %p
          #GroupActions.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+actions"}> group actions
                \/
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"}> G-sets
                )
              %br/
              Specializating Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BaseChangeOfPresheavesAlongFullyFaithfulFunctor"}
              to the case (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo =
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} =
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\,\mathcal{S} \longrightarrow \mathcal{S}'
              is the
              = succeed "-inclusion" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+category"} point
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mover
                      %mo ↪
                      %mphantom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo −
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    pt_{\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,\colon\,
                    \\ast
                    \\overset{\phantom{---}}{\hookrightarrow}
                    \\mathbf{B}G
                    \\,.
            %p
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping+groupoid"} delooping groupoid
              of a (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"}> discrete
              )
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh\big(\ast \big) \;\simeq\;
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≃
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh\big(\mathbf{B}G \big) \;\simeq\;
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                    Sets
                %p
                  is the category
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+actions"} group actions
                  with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+functions"} equivariant functions
                  between them,
            %p
              gives that
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BaseChangeOfPresheavesAsMonadicFunctor"} (1)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mi Sets
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mphantom
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo −
                    %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (pt_{\mathbf{B}G})^\ast
                    \\,\colon\,
                    G Sets \overset{\phantom{--}}{\longrightarrow} Sets
            %p
              which is hence
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sets
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \,\coloneqq\, G \times (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Sets \longrightarrow Sets
            %p
              which forms the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              with (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T \circ T
                    \\,=\,
                    G \times G \times (-)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    G \times (-)
                    \\,=\,
                    T
            %p is given by the group operation.
          %p
          #MonoidActions.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+actions"} monoid actions
                and monoid-oid actions)
              %br/
              In generalization of Ex.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GroupActions"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\, \mathcal{S} \longrightarrow \mathcal{S}'
              in Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BaseChangeOfPresheavesAlongFullyFaithfulFunctor"}
              is the point inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi pt
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo *
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    pt \,\colon\,\ast \longrightarrow \mathbf{B}A
            %p
              into the corresponding 1-object category (see
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "monoid#AsAOneObjectCategory"} there
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BaseChangeOfPresheavesAsMonadicFunctor"} (1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi pt
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi A
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mi Sets
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Sets
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (pt_{\mathbf{B}A})^\ast
                    \\;\colon\;
                    A Sets \longrightarrow Sets
            %p
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid+actions"} monoid actions
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
              of the monad
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \times (-)
            %p
              In this sense, the general situation of Ex.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BaseChangeOfPresheavesAlongFullyFaithfulFunctor"}
              may be understood as monadicity of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              for a
              %a{:href => "horizontal+categorification#Monoidoid"} monoid-oid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒮
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}'
              defined over a
              %a{:href => "horizontal+categorification#Monoidoid"} monoid-oid
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒮
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{S}
          %h3#GroupsOverSets Groups over sets
          %p
            We will use Duskin’s monadicity theorem (Thm.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DuskinMonadicityTheorem"}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi Grps
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mphantom
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo −
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi Sets
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  U
                  \\,\colon\,
                  Grps
                  \\overset{\phantom{---}}{\longrightarrow}
                  Sets
          %p
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Groups"} Groups
            to their underlying
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic
            = succeed "Of" do
              %br/
          %p
            We first need it to have a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+groups"} free groups
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
          %p
            It is also easy to show that it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conservative+functor"} conservative
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
            is a group isomorphism).
          %p So it remains to consider congruences:
          %p
            Since
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} created
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/congruence"} congruence
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Grp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp
            on a group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            which is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ×
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G\times G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ∼
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1\sim g_2
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_1\sim h_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mn 1
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo ∼
                  %msubsup
                    %mi g
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1^{-1}\sim g_2^{-1}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∼
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g_1 h_1 \sim g_2 h_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\sim g
            for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∼
                  %mi h
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\sim h
            if and only if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi h
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\sim h g^{-1}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim
            is determined by the subset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H\subseteq G
            of those
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\in G
            such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ∼
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\sim h
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            is clearly a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normal+subgroup"} normal subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\in H
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\in G
            we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∼
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi h
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 = g^{-1} g \sim g^{-1} h g
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi h
                    %mi g
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g^{-1} h g\in H
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Grp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Grp
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            Thus, by Duskin’s monadicity theorem (Thm.
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DuskinMonadicityTheorem"}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is monadic.
          %h3#categories_over_computads Categories over computads
          %p
            The monadicity theorem becomes more important when the base category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is more complicated and harder to work with explicitly, and when the objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are not obviously defined as “objects of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with extra structure.” For instance, the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-categories"} strict 2-categories
            is monadic over the category of 2-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/globular+sets"}> globular sets
            , essentially by definition, but it is much less trivial to show that it is
            %em also
            monadic over the category of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-computads"} 2-computads
          %h3#monadic_descent Monadic descent
          %p
            The monadicity theorem also plays a central role in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
          %h2#InInfinityCategories
            In
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            There is a version of the monadicity theorem for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-monads"} (∞,1)-monads
            in
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0702/0702299v5.pdf#page=107"} section 3.4
            of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em Noncommutative algebra
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0702299"}> arXiv
              )
          %p There is also a 2-categorical approach using quasicategories in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
              %em The 2-category theory of quasi-categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1306.5144"}> arXiv
              ),
              %em Homotopy coherent adjunctions and the formal theory of monads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.8279"}> arXiv
              )
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"}> monadic functor
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonadic+functor"} comonadic functor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+of+descent+type"} functor of descent type
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+decomposition"} monadic decomposition
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B%C3%A9nabou-Roubaud%27s+theorem"} Bénabou-Roubaud's theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+descent"} monadic descent
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The original reference for the (crude and precise) monadicity theorems is an untitled manuscript of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jon+Beck"} Jon Beck
            that was distributed around 1966 – 1968.
          %p
            A scan of a copy distributed at the
            %em Conference Held at the Seattle Research Center of the Battelle Memorial Institute
            in June – July 1968, provided by John Kennison:
          %ul
            %li#Beck68
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jon+Beck"}> Jon Beck
              , untitled manuscript (1968) &amp;lbrack;
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Beck_MonadicityTheorem.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A retyped reprint:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Mock+Beck"}> Jonathan Mock Beck
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em The tripleableness theorem
              %strong 31
              (2024) 1-11 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/31/tr31abs.html"}> tac:tr31
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/31/tr31.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"}> Michael Barr
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Coalgebras in a category of algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %em Category Theory, Homology Theory and their Applications I
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 86
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0079381"} doi:10.1007/BFb0079381
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#MacLane71
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+MacLane"}> Saunders MacLane
                , §VI.7 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+for+the+Working+Mathematician"} Categories for the Working Mathematician
                %strong 5
                Springer (1971) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4721-8
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Borceux
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                , Section 4 in volume 2 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
            %li#BarrWells
              %p
                Chapter 3 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Barr"} Michael Barr
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Wells"} Charles Wells
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Toposes%2C+Triples%2C+and+Theories"} Toposes, Triples, and Theories
                Grundlehren der math. Wissenschaften 278, Springer-Verlag 1983. Available as
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/12/tr12abs.html"} TAC Reprint 12
          %p Further references:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA+explained"}> FGA explained
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA+1"} SGA 1
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Linton"}> Fred Linton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Some aspects of equational categories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-99902-4_3"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-99902-4_3
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jack+Duskin"}> Jack Duskin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variations on Beck’s tripleability criterion
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Reports of the Midwest Category Seminar III
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 106
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0059143"} doi:10.1007/BFb0059143
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Linton"}> Fred Linton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Applied functorial semantics, I
                %strong 86
                (1970) 1-13 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02415703"}> doi:10.1007/BF02415703
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fred+Linton"}> Fred Linton
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Applied functorial semantics, II
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Seminar+on+Triples+and+Categorical+Homology+Theory"}> Seminar on Triples and Categorical Homology Theory
                    \: ETH 1966/67
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 80
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0083081"} doi:10.1007/BFb0083081
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"} Brian Day
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A monadicity theorem
                %strong 17
                2 (1977) 291-296 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/S0004972700010480"}> doi:10.1017/S0004972700010480
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Yasuo Kawahara,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A Relation Theoretic Proof of a Tripleability Theorem Over Exact Categories
                %strong 25
                (1978) 31-40 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://core.ac.uk/download/pdf/147423834.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Day"} Brian Day
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Universal algebra in a closed category
                %strong 16
                2 (1980) 133-147 [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(80)90012-2"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(80)90012-2
                ]
            %li#BenabouRoubaud70
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Roubaud"} Jacques Roubaud
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Monades et descente
                %strong 270
                (1970) 96-98 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://gallica.bnf.fr/ark:/12148/bpt6k480298g/f100"}> gallica:12148/bpt6k480298g/f100
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BenabouRoubaud-MonadesEtDescente.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "):" do
