                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/q/279152"} MO:q/279152
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Du%C5%A1ko+Pavlovi%C4%87"}> Duško Pavlović
                , Categorical interpolation: descent and the Beck-Chevalley condition without direct images, Category theory Como 1990, pp. 306–325, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1488, Springer 1991
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Deligne"}> Pierre Deligne
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat%C3%A9gories+Tannakiennes"} Catégories Tannakiennes
                , Grothendieck Festschrift, vol. II, Birkhäuser Progress in Math. 87 (1990) pp. 111-195.
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia:
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beck%27s_monadicity_theorem"} monadicity theorem
            %li
              %p
                John Bourke,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Two dimensional monadicity
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.5123"} arxiv/1212.5123
            %li#Riehl17
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
                , §5.5 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Category+Theory+in+Context"} Category Theory in Context
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://emilyriehl.github.io/files/context.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.jhu.edu/~eriehl/context/"} book website
          %p
            There is a version for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+contexts"} Morita contexts
            instead of monads:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tomasz+Brzezinski"}> Tomasz Brzezinski
              , Adrian Vazquez Marquez, Joost Vercruysse,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Eilenberg-Moore category and a Beck-type theorem for a Morita context
              %strong 19
              (2011), no. 5, 821–858
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=2836546"} MR2836546
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s10485-009-9217-0"} doi
          %p
            On Beck’s theorem for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudomonads"} pseudomonads
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+monadic+descent"} higher monadic descent
            for more details):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                I. J. Le Creurer,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francisco+Marmolejo"} Francisco Marmolejo
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Enrico+M.+Vitale"} Enrico M. Vitale
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Beck’s theorem for pseudo-monads
                %strong 173
                3 (2002) 293-313 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00038-5"}> doi:10.1016/S0022-4049(02)00038-5
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Claudio+Hermida"}> Claudio Hermida
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Descent on 2-fibrations and strongly 2-regular 2-categories
                %strong 12
                5-6 (2004) 427-459 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1023/B:APCS.0000049311.17100.da"}> doi:10.1023/B:APCS.0000049311.17100.da
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-monads"} (infinity,1)-monads
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              , section 4.7 of
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Algebra"} Higher Algebra
          %p
            and realized in the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
          %ul
            %li#RiehlVerity13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dominic+Verity"} Dominic Verity
              %em Homotopy coherent adjunctions and the formal theory of monads
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1310.8279"}> arXiv:1310.8279
              )
          %p Generalisation to “semads” (which are monads without units):
